TYPE UDT_PusherStim
  ROOTID 0
  COMMENT "Command and published state of the pusher stimulus head. The harness writes the command members before an index starts and reads the published ones while it runs. Each of the eight commanded plant signals is a two-edge timeline: it holds its Initial level until Edge1, takes the opposite level from Edge1 to Edge2, and returns to Initial at Edge2 - so one member set expresses hold, step, pulse and gap without the head knowing what any scenario is for. Every time is a duration measured from the start of the scenario, which is the instant the head cleardown finishes, never from Start. An edge time at or past EndAt is how a timeline says the signal never changes."
  MEMBERS
    Start : Bool COMMENT "In (harness): the index start bool. Its rising edge begins the head cleardown; its falling edge does not truncate an index, which ends only by reaching TailEnd."
    ScenarioDone : Bool COMMENT "Out: the index reached TailEnd. Latched, so a harness that was not polling at that instant still sees that it finished."
    EndAt : Time COMMENT "In (harness): how long the scenario itself lasts, measured from the start of the scenario. The head cleardown before it and the tail cleardown after it are the head's own fixed dwells and are not included."
    ResetAt : Time COMMENT "In (harness): when the fault-reset pulse is asserted inside the scenario under ResetMode 1, measured from the start of the scenario."
    ResetMode : Int COMMENT "In (harness): 0 never asserts the fault reset inside the scenario; 1 pulses it once at ResetAt; 2 holds it true throughout, so an edge-triggered reset finds no edge."
    ResetRequest : Bool COMMENT "Out: this head is asking for the plant fault-reset line. It is a REQUEST and not the line itself, because the hopper head drives the same line: the head publishes here and one authored rung arbitrates, passing the other head's value through whenever this index is not running."
    ArrivedDirty : Bool COMMENT "Out: a latched cause was already standing when this index began, before the head cleardown had done anything. Not a verdict on the block - a verdict on what the previous index left behind."
    InertAtStart : Bool COMMENT "Out: the head cleardown succeeded and the block held no latched cause when the scenario began. False means the scenario ran against a block that was not clean, so its result says nothing."
    RecoverFailed : Bool COMMENT "Out: a latched cause was still standing after the tail cleardown, so the block could not be returned to rest by a reset - which is a finding about the block, not about the index."
    InertAtEnd : Bool COMMENT "Out: the tail cleardown left the block with no latched cause, so the next index starts clean."
    Armed : Bool COMMENT "Out: the observation window is open. Published so the copy layer's observation latches are armed by this head's phase and not from the start of the index - a free-running latch would fill from the cleardown, where the block is legitimately being driven."
    ArmAt : Time COMMENT "In (harness): start of the observation window, measured from the start of the scenario."
    ArmUntil : Time COMMENT "In (harness): end of the observation window."
    Phase : Int COMMENT "Out: which index phase is running, positional - 1 head disarm, 2 head reset, 3 head verify, 4 scenario, 5 tail disarm, 6 tail reset, 7 tail verify, 0 between indexes. The codes are this head's own; never decode them against another head's."
    Mode : Int COMMENT "In (harness): the operator pusher mode presented for the whole scenario - 0 Off, 1 Auto, 2 Manual. Reaches the block through DB_Controls.PusherMode and the sequencer's PusherModeCmd, so it is honoured only while the sequencer's own PusherModeForceOff is clear."
    HopperInitial : Bool COMMENT "In (harness): the level the hopper high-level sensor holds from the start of the scenario until Edge1."
    HopperEdge1 : Time COMMENT "In (harness): when the hopper high-level sensor leaves its initial level, measured from the start of the scenario. A time at or past EndAt means it never does."
    HopperEdge2 : Time COMMENT "In (harness): when the hopper high-level sensor returns to its initial level, measured from the start of the scenario. A time at or past EndAt means it never does."
    ManualCycleInitial : Bool COMMENT "In (harness): the level the operator manual-cycle button holds from the start of the scenario until Edge1."
    ManualCycleEdge1 : Time COMMENT "In (harness): when the operator manual-cycle button leaves its initial level, measured from the start of the scenario. A time at or past EndAt means it never does."
    ManualCycleEdge2 : Time COMMENT "In (harness): when the operator manual-cycle button returns to its initial level, measured from the start of the scenario. A time at or past EndAt means it never does."
    JogExtendInitial : Bool COMMENT "In (harness): the level the operator jog-extend button holds from the start of the scenario until Edge1."
    JogExtendEdge1 : Time COMMENT "In (harness): when the operator jog-extend button leaves its initial level, measured from the start of the scenario. A time at or past EndAt means it never does."
    JogExtendEdge2 : Time COMMENT "In (harness): when the operator jog-extend button returns to its initial level, measured from the start of the scenario. A time at or past EndAt means it never does."
    JogRetractInitial : Bool COMMENT "In (harness): the level the operator jog-retract button holds from the start of the scenario until Edge1."
    JogRetractEdge1 : Time COMMENT "In (harness): when the operator jog-retract button leaves its initial level, measured from the start of the scenario. A time at or past EndAt means it never does."
    JogRetractEdge2 : Time COMMENT "In (harness): when the operator jog-retract button returns to its initial level, measured from the start of the scenario. A time at or past EndAt means it never does."
    HomeInitial : Bool COMMENT "In (harness): the level the home limit switch holds from the start of the scenario until Edge1."
    HomeEdge1 : Time COMMENT "In (harness): when the home limit switch leaves its initial level, measured from the start of the scenario. A time at or past EndAt means it never does."
    HomeEdge2 : Time COMMENT "In (harness): when the home limit switch returns to its initial level, measured from the start of the scenario. A time at or past EndAt means it never does."
    FullTravelInitial : Bool COMMENT "In (harness): the level the full-travel limit switch holds from the start of the scenario until Edge1."
    FullTravelEdge1 : Time COMMENT "In (harness): when the full-travel limit switch leaves its initial level, measured from the start of the scenario. A time at or past EndAt means it never does."
    FullTravelEdge2 : Time COMMENT "In (harness): when the full-travel limit switch returns to its initial level, measured from the start of the scenario. A time at or past EndAt means it never does."
    HighPressureInitial : Bool COMMENT "In (harness): the level the high-pressure switch holds from the start of the scenario until Edge1."
    HighPressureEdge1 : Time COMMENT "In (harness): when the high-pressure switch leaves its initial level, measured from the start of the scenario. A time at or past EndAt means it never does."
    HighPressureEdge2 : Time COMMENT "In (harness): when the high-pressure switch returns to its initial level, measured from the start of the scenario. A time at or past EndAt means it never does."
    PackRunningInitial : Bool COMMENT "In (harness): the level the power-pack running feedback holds from the start of the scenario until Edge1."
    PackRunningEdge1 : Time COMMENT "In (harness): when the power-pack running feedback leaves its initial level, measured from the start of the scenario. A time at or past EndAt means it never does."
    PackRunningEdge2 : Time COMMENT "In (harness): when the power-pack running feedback returns to its initial level, measured from the start of the scenario. A time at or past EndAt means it never does."
    HealthyInitial : Bool COMMENT "In (harness): the level the control-circuit healthy input holds from the start of the scenario until Edge1."
    HealthyEdge1 : Time COMMENT "In (harness): when the control-circuit healthy input leaves its initial level, measured from the start of the scenario. A time at or past EndAt means it never does."
    HealthyEdge2 : Time COMMENT "In (harness): when the control-circuit healthy input returns to its initial level, measured from the start of the scenario. A time at or past EndAt means it never does."
    DownstreamInitial : Bool COMMENT "In (harness): the level the downstream-running input holds from the start of the scenario until Edge1."
    DownstreamEdge1 : Time COMMENT "In (harness): when the downstream-running input leaves its initial level, measured from the start of the scenario. A time at or past EndAt means it never does."
    DownstreamEdge2 : Time COMMENT "In (harness): when the downstream-running input returns to its initial level, measured from the start of the scenario. A time at or past EndAt means it never does."
